<title>BELGIUM: Belgian forex reserves up 1.4 bln Bfr due Ecu swap.</title>
<headline>Belgian forex reserves up 1.4 bln Bfr due Ecu swap.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian National Bank said its foreign exchange reserves rose 1.4 billion Belgian francs in the week to Monday due mainly to its quarterly Ecu swap with the European Monetary Institute. Separately, the BNB said money market support was increased. (figures in bln francs):</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   411.097 (+ 1.358)</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security   7.975 (- 1.942)</p>
<p> Commercial bills			  3.239 (- 0.128)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio		   23.319 (+ 0.002)</p>
<p> Money market interventions	  112.324 (+ 3.041)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   447.665 (- 0.158)</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710 $ $</p>
